=========================================================
STRUCTURAL DESIGN PATTERNS - MOST ASKED INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
=========================================================

=========================================================
1. What is a Structural Design Pattern?
=========================================================

Structural patterns explain how classes and objects are
combined to form larger, flexible and maintainable systems.

=========================================================
2. Adapter vs Facade
=========================================================

Adapter
--------
• Converts one interface into another.
• Makes incompatible classes work together.
• Usually wraps one existing class.

Example:
XML → JSON Converter

Facade
-------
• Provides a simplified interface to a complex subsystem.
• Does NOT change the interface.
• Hides complexity from the client.

Example:
Order Processing System

Interview Line:
Adapter changes the interface.
Facade simplifies the interface.

=========================================================
3. Decorator vs Proxy
=========================================================

Decorator
----------
• Adds new behavior dynamically.
• Focus is extending functionality.

Example:
Pizza + Cheese + Olives

Proxy
------
• Controls access to an object.
• Focus is authentication, authorization,
  lazy loading, logging, caching.

Example:
Folder Access Permission

Interview Line:
Decorator adds functionality.
Proxy controls access.

=========================================================
4. Bridge vs Adapter
=========================================================

Bridge
-------
• Separates abstraction from implementation.
• Designed before the system is built.
• Prevents class explosion.

Example:
Shape + Color

Adapter
--------
• Makes incompatible classes work together.
• Usually applied after classes already exist.

Example:
XML → JSON Converter

Interview Line:
Bridge separates two independent hierarchies.
Adapter connects incompatible interfaces.

=========================================================
5. Why use composition instead of inheritance?
=========================================================

Composition provides:
• Loose coupling
• Better flexibility
• Runtime behavior changes
• Better extensibility

Inheritance creates tight coupling and often leads to
class explosion.

=========================================================
6. Why Bridge instead of inheritance?
=========================================================

Inheritance creates classes like:

RedCircle
BlueCircle
GreenCircle
RedRectangle
BlueRectangle

Bridge separates:

Shape
Color

and combines them using composition.

Result:
No class explosion.

=========================================================
7. Why not implement access control inside the real object instead of Proxy?
=========================================================

Because access control is a separate responsibility.

Real Object:
• Business logic only

Proxy:
• Authentication
• Authorization
• Logging
• Lazy loading

This follows Single Responsibility Principle.

=========================================================
8. Types of Proxy
=========================================================

• Protection Proxy
  → Access control

• Virtual Proxy
  → Lazy initialization

• Remote Proxy
  → Access remote object

• Cache Proxy
  → Cache expensive results

=========================================================
9. Why use Decorator instead of inheritance?
=========================================================

Inheritance:

CheesePizza
OlivePizza
CheeseOlivePizza
CheeseOliveMushroomPizza

Decorator:

Pizza
 + Cheese
 + Olives
 + Mushroom

Behavior can be added dynamically.

=========================================================
10. What problem does Facade solve?
=========================================================

Facade hides the complexity of multiple subsystems by
providing a single simple interface.

Instead of:

Payment
Inventory
Shipping
Notification

Client simply calls:

placeOrder()

=========================================================
11. What problem does Adapter solve?
=========================================================

Adapter allows incompatible interfaces to work together
without modifying existing code.

Example:

Existing System → XML

New Tool → JSON

Adapter converts XML → JSON.

=========================================================
12. What problem does Bridge solve?
=========================================================

Bridge avoids class explosion by separating two
independent dimensions and connecting them using
composition.

=========================================================
13. What problem does Proxy solve?
=========================================================

Proxy controls access to an object by acting as an
intermediate layer.

It can provide:
• Security
• Logging
• Lazy loading
• Caching

=========================================================
14. Which Structural Patterns use Composition?
=========================================================

✔ Adapter
✔ Decorator
✔ Proxy
✔ Bridge
✔ Facade

Most structural patterns prefer composition over
inheritance.

=========================================================
15. One-line Definitions
=========================================================

Adapter
→ Converts one interface into another.

Decorator
→ Adds new behavior dynamically.

Facade
→ Provides a simple interface to a complex subsystem.

Proxy
→ Controls access to another object.

Bridge
→ Separates abstraction from implementation so both
can vary independently.

